# FIELD Platform — environment template. Copy to .env; never commit .env.
# No real credentials anywhere in this repo. All values below are local-dev defaults.

# --- Compose stack: ONE published port (integration/demo/Caddyfile) ---
# The docker-compose stack publishes only the Caddy proxy on 8080 (GB10:
# 18080). Every service is a path prefix behind it; the proxy strips the
# prefix so apps still see root paths. Host-side callers (CLIs, field-agent
# SDK, attestation/lifecycle jobs) point their FIELD_*_URL vars at:
#   FIELD_REGISTRY_URL=http://localhost:8080/registry
#   FIELD_LEDGER_URL=http://localhost:8080/ledger
#   FIELD_DELEGATION_URL=http://localhost:8080/delegation
#   FIELD_SENTINEL_URL=http://localhost:8080/sentinel
#   FIELD_KILLSWITCH_URL=http://localhost:8080/killswitch
#   FIELD_GOVERNOR_URL=http://localhost:8080/governor
#   FIELD_REPLAY_URL=http://localhost:8080/replay
#   FIELD_GATEWAY_URL=http://localhost:8080/gateway
#   FIELD_FEDERATION_URL=http://localhost:8080/federation
#   FIELD_LIFECYCLE_URL=http://localhost:8080/lifecycle
#   FIELD_ATTEST_URL=http://localhost:8080/attest
#   FIELD_CROSSWALK_URL=http://localhost:8080/crosswalk
#   ops-console (dashboard) is the proxy ROOT: http://localhost:8080/
# The no-docker local path (run_demo.sh / per-service demo.sh) still serves
# per-service ports 8001-8013 directly; code defaults are unchanged.
# NOTE: interactive Swagger /docs pages 404 behind the stripped prefixes
# (they fetch /openapi.json root-absolute); API traffic is unaffected.

# federation-broker: our org name as counterparty manifests must declare it
FIELD_ORG_NAME=Spin State Labs

# --- Inter-service authn (OQ-1) ---
# Unset = localhost-trust demo mode. Set the SAME value in every service's
# and client's environment to require x-field-auth on all endpoints except
# /health. Generate one: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
# FIELD_SHARED_SECRET=

# --- Data directories (default: ./var inside each service) ---
FIELD_DATA_DIR=./var

# NOTE: for the compose stack this file must be copied to integration/demo/.env
# — Compose reads .env from the compose file directory, never from the repo
# root, so `cp .env.example .env` here reaches no container.
# --- Operator passthroughs (v1.2 A0) ---
# compose forwards NO host env on its own; each variable below has a
# ${VAR:-default} line in integration/demo/docker-compose.yml (and an export
# in integration/fly/entrypoint.sh), so setting it in the estate .env is
# enough — no compose edit at deploy time. Paths are CONTAINER paths (/data).
# lifecycle-manager scheduler: seconds between sweeps (0 = off; compose/Fly
# default 86400 = daily). A tick with no roster is logged as skipped.
FIELD_LIFECYCLE_EVERY=86400
# compliance-crosswalk scheduler: seconds between runs (compose/Fly default
# 86400 = daily; the scheduler itself lands in D4).
FIELD_CROSSWALK_EVERY=86400
# HR owner roster CSV (`owner` column) the lifecycle sweep reads when no
# roster is posted; put the file on the /data volume. Unset = no sweep runs.
# Rosters go directly under /data, NEVER under /data/manifests: on the GB10
# from v1.2 Phase C that path is the read-only field-manifests volume, whose
# only writer (manifests-admin install) accepts FIELD manifests and nothing
# else, so a roster there could never be changed again.
# FIELD_LIFECYCLE_ROSTER=/data/owners.csv
# Delegation-of-authority roster for the grantor check. READ on every mint.
# YAML, not CSV — see manifests/doa-roster.example.yaml. Setting this ARMS a
# fail-closed gate: an unreadable or invalid file makes every mint 503.
# FIELD_DOA_ROSTER=/data/doa-roster.yaml
# Kill-endpoint allowlist — comma-separated hosts the kill-switch may signal.
# READ on every kill. Unset = no agent endpoint is ever called. It gates the
# HOST, not the path or the method. WARNING: with a live agent host listed, a
# `/drill` sends that agent a REAL halt signal — the registry status is
# restored, the signal cannot be.
# FIELD_KILL_ENDPOINT_ALLOWLIST=
# Estate ledger retention policy in days; 2555 = seven years (compose/Fly
# default). GET /ledger/retention/check compares every registered manifest's
# ledger.retention_days (a floor the estate must meet) against it. Unset on a
# bare install = "no estate policy" (ledger retention check exits 3).
# FIELD_LEDGER_RETENTION_DAYS=2555
# Ledger rotation signing key (C2): a PEM PATH under /data, never key material.
# UNSET by default — POST /ledger/rotate answers 503 "no anchor key configured"
# (never an unsigned rotation) until arming step A4 generates the key in-estate
# and sets the path.
# FIELD_LEDGER_ANCHOR_KEY=/data/keys/ledger-anchor.pem
# X4 witness (GB10 compose `witness` service, profile `witness`), armed at A5 by
# BOTH lines below in integration/demo/.env; without the profile no `up` starts
# it. FIELD_WITNESS_EVERY: seconds between ticks; lifecycle reports a finding
# when the latest anchor.remote{estate: fly} is older than 3 x this. Unset or
# blank => no witness finding (Fly, and the GB10 before A5 or after disarm).
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=witness
# FIELD_WITNESS_EVERY=3600
# X4 direction 2, ONLY after D5: a path inside the witness container to a file
# holding Fly's FIELD_SHARED_SECRET. Unset = "direction 2 not live (D5)".
# FIELD_WITNESS_FLY_SECRET_FILE=
# Retention apply target for archived closed segments. Blank = $FIELD_DATA_DIR/
# ledger-archive. Must be under FIELD_DATA_DIR (else --allow-external), not
# inside the live ledger dir, and on the same filesystem (archival renames).
# FIELD_LEDGER_ARCHIVE_DIR=
# Base for relative manifest_ref paths inside the containers.
# FIELD_MANIFEST_DIR=/data/manifests
# FIELD_BUILD_SHA (v1.2 Phase C) does NOT belong in this file: it is a build
# arg baked into the image and reported as build_sha by every /health. Pass it
# on the build command line (FIELD_BUILD_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD) docker
# compose ... build); a value here would be baked, stale, into every build.
# force-gateway: 1 = deterministic keyless upstream (compose keeps --mock
# until D2; this passthrough lets the estate .env drive it afterwards).
# FORCE_GATEWAY_MOCK=

# --- force-gateway (Phase 3) — key is YOUR key, set only in your local .env ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Conformance sentinel operating mode (S1 / ADR 02 safety ordering) ---
# Unset or "log_only" = safe-by-default: verdicts are shadow-ledgered as
# would-block/would-escalate but never enforced (the estate observes first).
# "enforce" = verdicts block/escalate for real. Graduate to enforce only after
# the measured gate (catch >= 95%, false-block <= 2%).
# NOTE: any unrecognized value silently falls back to log_only (fail-safe
# direction, but silent) — verify GET /health reports the mode you intended.
# FIELD_SENTINEL_MODE=log_only

# --- Sentinel semantic judge (S3 / ADR 02) — default OFF ---
# off (or unset) = structural-only, S2-identical behavior. "mock" = the
# deterministic keyless mock (tests/demos). "anthropic" = the real pinned
# model (needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; spend-metered to the sentinel's own
# governor cap — no cap, no judgments). Unrecognized values fall back to off.
# FIELD_SENTINEL_JUDGE=off
# FIELD_JUDGE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# FIELD_JUDGE_CONFIDENCE_FLOOR=0.8

# --- FORCE Gateway delta (ADR 10) — sampled hygiene judge, default OFF ---
# The gateway is an OBSERVER that fails open: its faults bypass, never block.
# Judge: off (unset) | mock (keyless) | anthropic (needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY;
# metered to the gateway's own cap — governor set-cap force-gateway
# --from-manifest). Unrecognized values fall back to off.
# FORCE_HYGIENE_JUDGE=off
# FORCE_HYGIENE_JUDGE_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# FORCE_GATEWAY_SAMPLE_EVERY=10      # deterministic 1-in-N sampling; 0=off
# FORCE_HYGIENE_WINDOW=5             # judged scores per drift window
# FORCE_HYGIENE_BAND=0.15            # baseline +/- band
# FORCE_HYGIENE_BASELINE_WINDOWS=2   # windows that fix the baseline
# FORCE_GATEWAY_LATENCY_BUDGET_MS=250   # instrumentation overhead budget
# FORCE_GATEWAY_BYPASS_COOLDOWN=10   # uninstrumented requests per bypass

# --- Compliance Crosswalk delta (ADR 07) — gated suggestions, default OFF ---
# Suggestions are SUGGESTION ONLY (human sign-off gate); below the precision
# floor renders as "unmapped — review required", never as a mapping. off
# (unset) | mock (keyless) | anthropic (needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY + a governor
# cap for compliance-crosswalk — no unmetered LLM calls). Unrecognized -> off.
# Stale flags live at $FIELD_DATA_DIR/crosswalk_stale_flags.json; a stale
# framework hard-blocks evidence-pack generation until a NAMED re-review.
# CROSSWALK_SUGGEST=off
# CROSSWALK_SUGGEST_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# CROSSWALK_SUGGEST_FLOOR=0.8
